# git-blame ignore list
#
# This file lists commits that should be ignored by `git blame` because
# they are pure, mechanical reformatting and not meaningful content
# changes. Ignoring them keeps blame pointing at the commit that
# actually introduced a line's logic, instead of the reformat commit.
#
# This file alone does nothing: git only reads it when you tell it to,
# either per-invocation with `git blame --ignore-revs-file
# .git-blame-ignore-revs`, or persistently with:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# GitHub's web blame view also honors this file automatically.

